C6 = ( u1 ∨ u2 ∨ u4), C7 = ( u2 ∨ u3 ∨ u4), and C8 = ( u1 ∨ u3 ∨ u4). By deﬁnition, S is an
instance of 3-SAT. The gadget graph GS is given in Figure 2.
Since each literal occurs as often as its negation, and each c lause has three literals, the
number of clauses in S must be even. Hence, m = 2 k for some integer k ≥ 1. From the
instance S, we will deﬁne a set XS with 18 k vertices corresponding to the teams in league
