Following the convention of the TTP (Easton, Nemhauser, & Tr ick, 2002), we deﬁne
ILB t to be the individual lower bound for team t. This value represents the minimum
possible distance that can be traveled by team t in order to complete all of their games
under the constraints of BTTP, independent of the other teams’ schedules. By deﬁnition,
for each team t located at y ∈ YS, the value of ILB t is the minimum weight of a y-rooted
4-cycle-cover.
Similarly, we deﬁne the league lower bound LLBT to be the minimum possible distance
traveled by all of the teams t in league T , and the tournament lower bound T LB to be the
minimum possible distance traveled by all the teams in both l eagues. We note the following
trivial inequalities:
