distance ≤ T (k) iﬀ the instance S with 2k clauses is satisﬁable. This establishes the desired
polynomial-time reduction from 3-SAT, proving the NP-hard ness of BTTP and BTTP*.
Finally, we note that both problems are clearly in NP, since t he distance traveled by the
teams can be calculated in polynomial time. Therefore, we co nclude that BTTP and BTTP*
are NP-complete.
