codex
The workspace also contained an independently produced implementation for this same paper, and it is materially stronger than the first draft: it returns a two-coefficient finite-field functional, expands its fibers into the paper’s uniform triplet schedule, and explicitly checks every BTTP constraint. I’m preserving that newer work rather than overwriting it. Its current local report passes all gates with a fixed two-atom answer, a 976,500-operation exact reference scan, and a 255-operation invariant route; I’m now auditing the construction and waiting for the concurrent file writer to settle before regenerating the script-owned transcripts.
