@@ -0,0 +1,217 @@
+# arXiv:1401.3909 — verified triplet-road scheduler generator
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | optimization |
+| Object regime | finite field (with an exact integer venue metric) |
+| Computational core | exact cover |
+| Certificate | exact symbolic linear functional `[a,b]` over GF(p) |
+| Intuition | invariant: the global tag sum is orthogonal to the triplet functional |
+| Domain essentiality | licensed reduction |
+| Reduction | paper-licensed, Section 5 triplet packing → uniform BTTP* schedule |
+
+This is representational coverage of the paper's scheduling construction, not a
+claim that the solver manipulates an unrestricted BTTP instance.  The surrogate
+is licensed by Section 5, but the added finite-field compression is specific to
+this benchmark family.
+
+## What the problem is and whether to trust it
+
+[Hoshino and Kawarabayashi, *Scheduling Bipartite Tournaments to Minimize Total
+Travel Distance*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.3909) define the Bipartite Traveling
+Tournament Problem (BTTP).  Two leagues of `n` teams play every cross-league
+pair twice, once at each venue, in `2n` slots.  Home/away runs have length at
+most three and opponents cannot repeat in consecutive slots.  Section 5 builds
+a uniform schedule by partitioning each league into road-trip triples and
+pairing triples through cyclic three-slot blocks.
+
+The instance supplies one league's compressed, exact venue metric and a
+two-coordinate tag for every team.  The answer `[a,b]` defines the key
+`K(i)=a*u_i+b*v_i mod p`; its fibers must be triples.  `verify` expands those
+fibers into all `2n` rounds, checks each-venue, no-repeat, at-most-three, and
+uniformity, then sums the integer travel expression and compares it to the
+inclusive target.  It never reads `inst["answer"]`.
+
+Generation is inverse, not search.  The coefficients are sampled first.  Three
+points are placed on each affine fiber, fiber values are chosen to sum to zero,
+and a tree metric is assembled around those fibers.  A true triplet has no
+center-to-root penalty; every mixed triplet has a positive one.  This proves the
+planted fibers uniquely minimize the triplet partition, while every nonzero
+scalar multiple of the coefficient vector is a valid symbolic certificate.
+
+## Why this is Track B
+
+Theorem 1 proves unrestricted BTTP and BTTP* NP-complete, but that worst-case
+result does not establish hardness for this distribution.  Section 4 also gives
+the easy boundary: Propositions 1 and 2 reduce/propagate the `n=6` NPB instance,
+which the authors solve exactly in 34,716 seconds.  Section 5's NBA method
+enumerates `15!/(5!*2^5) = 340,540,200` non-equivalent ordered triplet plans.
+
+For these planted metrics a polynomial reference algorithm exists and is
+reported honestly.  It tests whether every pair of distance rows differs by a
+constant outside the pair, costing `O(n^3)`.  At shipping `n=126`, it performs
+exactly 976,500 row-difference subtractions, solves 8/8 seeds, and took about
+0.05–0.09 seconds per instance locally.  The compact route notices that the
+global tag sum `(U,V)` is orthogonal to the hidden functional and returns
+`[V,-U] mod p`; its measured bound is 255 exact operations.  The benchmark asks
+whether a no-tool solver finds that compression, not whether software can solve
+the instance.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=0`)
+
+This smallest setting is hand-solvable: sum the six tag coordinates modulo 13
+to get `(2,10)`, so `[10,11]` is perpendicular to the sum.  The complete
+rendered instance is:
+
+```text
+Bipartite triplet-road scheduling (arXiv:1401.3909, Section 5)
+
+There are two leagues X and Y, each with n=6 teams, and m=2.
+The X teams are already partitioned into consecutive triples.  You must give a
+compact rule that partitions the 0-indexed Y teams 0,...,5 into
+triples.  The rule will be expanded into a uniform double round-robin schedule.
+
+Definitions.  A double round-robin bipartite schedule has 2n slots.  Every X-Y
+pair plays twice, once at each venue.  It is uniform when all X teams have the
+same home/away status in a slot.  No team may have more than three consecutive
+home games or away games (the at-most-three rule), and no team may face the same
+opponent in consecutive slots (the no-repeat rule).
+
+Expansion template.  Treat each Y triple as one road-trip unit.  For block
+r=0,...,m-1, pair X triple g with Y triple (g+r) mod m for an X-home block, then
+with Y triple (g+r+2) mod m for a Y-home block.  Each block has three slots and
+uses the cyclic 3-by-3 matching: member q of the X triple faces member (q+s)
+mod 3 of the Y triple in subslot s.  This deterministically gives 2n slots and
+the checker explicitly verifies all three constraints above.
+
+Each Y team i has a public tag (u_i,v_i) over GF(p), where p=13.
+For your two coefficients [a,b], define
+    K(i) = (a*u_i + b*v_i) mod p.
+Teams with equal K(i) form one Y road-trip unit.  Your coefficients must be
+distinct residues in 0,...,p-1, and the fibers of K must be exactly m triples.
+
+Tags, as `team: u v`:
+0: 12 2
+1: 7 3
+2: 4 0
+3: 5 5
+4: 6 11
+5: 7 2
+
+The symmetric Y-venue distance matrix D has D(i,i)=0.  Its strict upper
+triangle is below: row i lists D(i,i+1), D(i,i+2), ..., D(i,n-1), in that order.
+All entries are exact nonnegative integers.
+0: 120447 143591 183762 160342 223852
+1: 63716 103887 80467 143977
+2: 120273 103611 160363
+3: 143782 200534
+4: 183872
+5: (empty)
+
+For a fiber {i,j,k}, its perimeter is D(i,j)+D(j,k)+D(k,i).  For the expanded
+uniform schedule, all other travel contributes the exact fixed amount
+F=39775512, and the exact total travel is
+    F + 4 * (sum of all fiber perimeters).
+The total must be at most T=43145216 (inclusive).  Fiber order and the
+order of teams inside a fiber do not affect this total.
+
+Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON array [a,b].
+Example syntax: <answer>[0, 1]</answer>
+Output nothing else inside the tags.
+```
+
+The planted answer is `<answer>[1, 5]</answer>` and
+`verify(inst, [1,5]) == (True, "ok")`.  The swapped corruption gives
+`verify(inst, [5,1]) == (False, "coefficient fibers are not all triples")`.
+The compact hand-derived answer `[10,11]` also verifies, demonstrating that the
+checker accepts witnesses other than the planted representation.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| Preset | n per league | p | reference row differences | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 6 | 13 | 60 | hand example |
+| easy | 18 | 1,000,003 | 2,448 | oracle unavailable |
+| medium | 60 | 10,000,019 | 102,660 | locally verified |
+| hard | 126 | 50,000,017 | 976,500 | **shipping preset; locally verified** |
+
+`escalate` increases the modulus and metric scale at fixed two-integer answer
+length.  Thus it grows coefficient entropy without lengthening the witness.
+
+## Gate results
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 20/20 preset/seed plants verified and JSON-round-tripped |
+| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged JSON recovered from fenced surrounding prose |
+| G4 | pass | 0/250,000 guesses; exact density `1/50,000,017` |
+| G5 | pass | 50,000,016 valid certificates of 2,500,001,650,000,272; reference cost 976,500 subtractions |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks at 0/8; reference algorithm solves 8/8 as Track B expects |
+| G7 | pass | doubled `n=252` builds/verifies; reference work rises to 7,906,500 with two answer atoms |
+| G8 | pass | 20/20 permutations, basis swaps, and compositions; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 19 chars, 5 estimated tokens, 2 atoms, 255 exact operations |
+
+The four failing attacks are closest-row-sum outlier selection,
+shortest-distance greedy selection, the by-hand `[1,1]` equal-tag-sum ansatz,
+and 256 random projective restarts.  An additional 500-seed audit found zero
+successes for all four.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+The required OpenRouter run was attempted, but the configured key returned HTTP
+403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` on every request.  The harness correctly
+records these as errors, not model failures.  Therefore **there is no oracle
+hardness verdict yet**, and this directory must not be represented as a fully
+hardened submission until the run is repeated with a usable key.
+
+| Run | Requested preset | Scored solved/attempts | Result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare | easy | 0/0 | four HTTP 403 errors; harness aborted |
+| structural hint | hard | 0/0 | four HTTP 403 errors; harness aborted |
+| placebo hint | hard | 0/0 | four HTTP 403 errors; harness aborted |
+
+`hinted - placebo` is consequently undefined.  The hint diagnostic cannot yet
+say whether naming global-sum orthogonality helps.  The size/effort part of G9
+still passes with the measurements above.  The error-only transcripts were
+written by `harden.py` and retained unedited.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_1401_3909 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, parse_answer, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+prompt = render(inst)
+answer = parse_answer("<answer>[0, 1]</answer>")
+ok, reason = verify(inst, answer)
+```
+
+From the repository root, emit JSONL after a successful oracle rerun with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1401.3909 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The exact guess density is for the declared prior: uniform distinct coefficient
+pairs, after enforcing the obvious two-residue syntax.  It does not model a
+solver that notices tag algebra.  Indeed, the intended invariant solves the
+family quickly; that is why this is Track B.  The metric itself also yields to
+the measured cubic row-profile scan in milliseconds with software.
+
+The benchmark compresses candidate-independent cross-league travel into `F`;
+it does not expose the unrestricted full `2n by 2n` BTTP distance matrix.  The
+checker does expand and inspect the full schedule combinatorics, but this is
+licensed-reduction rather than native-domain coverage.  The canonical key uses
+sorted weighted-row profiles, not complete weighted-graph canonization, so a
+rare non-isomorphic collision is theoretically possible.
+
+No external CP-SAT, MILP, simulated annealing, or hybrid CP/IP implementation
+was run.  The paper's Proposition 1 reduction-prior-to-propagation and
+Proposition 2 geographic special case were analyzed but not reimplemented,
+because this planted distribution has the stronger exact profile algorithm.
+Most importantly, the four-vendor oracle and all three G9 arms remain unscored
+until the OpenRouter quota is restored.
