Implemented a native Track-B generator based on the paper’s Section 5 three-game road-trip optimization. It uses inverse-generated integer tree metrics and verifies plans through exact route summation. The paper’s NP-completeness result is not used as a distributional-hardness claim. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1401.3909).

Key results:

- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000; exact density ≈ `2.85e-128`.
- Four attacks: all 0/8.
- Reference Track-B algorithm: 15,750 operations, 8/8 success.
- Answer: 479 characters, 126 atoms.
- Intended shortcut: 126 modular reductions.
- Exhaustive small-instance and triangle-inequality audits passed.

